# Data conversion between bit and kibibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between bit and kibibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1b to 0.0001KiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5b yields 0.0001KiB; backward, converting 1KiB to 8192b preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5KiB yields 12288.0b.

>>> source
const forward_whole: int = 1b
print(forward_whole->to(KiB))
const forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5b
print(forward_fractional->to(KiB))
const backward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(backward_whole->to(b))
const backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(backward_fractional->to(b))

<<< stdout
0.0001KiB
0.0001KiB
8192b
12288.0b

<<< stderr
